/// imported
state default-found: "Default Entered" by office cite cfr210.16.b.4
{
  group response-period-group
  note "Respondent is deemed to waive its right to appear, to be served with documents, and to contest the allegations at issue. Reached either from the response-window default track or from a case-dispositive discovery sanction below (cf. Certain Opaque Polymers, 337-TA-883 — Organik Kimya's spoliation drew case-dispositive default, affirmed by the Federal Circuit)."
  _ "Facts alleged in the complaint presumed true as to the defaulting respondent (Rule 210.16(c); § 1337(g))" -> default-relief-determination {
    authority cite cfr210.16.c
  }
}

/// imported
state default-relief-determination: "Default Relief Determination" by examiner cite usc1337.g
{
  group response-period-group
  note "Facts alleged in the complaint are presumed true as to the defaulting respondent. Default is not a free exit for the complainant's adversary: the Commission may still issue an exclusion order or cease-and-desist order against the defaulting respondent's imports, after considering public health and welfare, competitive conditions, and consumer interests (19 CFR 210.16(c))."
  _ "ALJ issues a violation ID on the presumed-true facts, after considering public health, competitive effects, and consumer interests (§ 1337(g))" -> violation-id {
    authority cite usc1337.g
  }
}

/// imported
decision discovery-open: "Discovery Open" by applicant cite cfr210.27.b
{
  group discovery-group
  note "Parties discover matters 'not privileged, that is proportional to the needs of the investigation' — broadly FRCP-26(b)(1)-shaped, but scoped to a 45-day-post-institution target date rather than a multi-year docket, with compressed 10-day response windows throughout. This hub node is a pure player node (every outgoing edge, including its self-loops, is an applicant choice) — the direct structural analog of mpep-prosecution.json's RCE-churn cycle: the SCC where time, money, and CBI risk accumulate before the case can graduate to prehearing."
  discovery-serve-interrogatories "Serve Interrogatories (≤175 including discrete subparts, Rule 210.29)" -> discovery-open {
    authority cite cfr210.29.limits
    effort 8.hours
    cost 200.usd
    action_id "serve.discovery.interrogatories"
  }
  discovery-respond-interrogatories-rfp "Respond to interrogatories or requests for production within 10 days — or risk sanction exposure (Rule 210.29; 210.30(b); 210.33(a))" -> discovery-open {
    authority cite cfr210.29.limits
    effort 35.hours
    cost 1_000.usd
    deadline 10.days {
      extendable true
      extension_authority "ALJ-specified period"
      note "19 CFR 210.29/210.30(b): 10 days to answer interrogatories or respond to document requests unless the ALJ specifies otherwise. A miss is sanction exposure under 210.33(a) — the pack does not assert an automatic waiver here, contrast the RFA trap below."
    }
    duration { min 1.5.days, mode 5.days, max 10.days }
  }
  discovery-serve-rfp "Serve Requests for Production (Rule 210.30)" -> discovery-open {
    authority cite cfr210.30.b
    effort 5.hours
    cost 150.usd
    action_id "serve.discovery.rfp"
  }
  discovery-serve-rfa "Serve Requests for Admission (Rule 210.31)" -> discovery-open {
    authority cite cfr210.31.b
    effort 3.hours
    cost 100.usd
    action_id "serve.discovery.rfa"
  }
  discovery-rfa-deemed-admitted "Fail to timely answer or object to a Request for Admission — deemed admitted (Rule 210.31(b))" -> discovery-open {
    authority cite cfr210.31.b
    effort 0.hours
    deadline 10.days {
      extendable true
      extension_authority "ALJ-specified period"
      note "19 CFR 210.31(b): deemed admitted absent a sworn answer or objection within 10 days or the ALJ-specified period. Flag itc337/rfa-deemed-admitted raised — the matter is conclusively established absent ALJ leave to withdraw or amend, and the respond.rfa action itself becomes illegal once the window closes."
    }
    duration { min 1.5.days, mode 5.days, max 10.days }
    valence bad
  }
  discovery-serve-subpoena "Serve Subpoena (Rule 210.32)" -> discovery-open {
    authority cite cfr210.32.a
    effort 4.hours
    cost 250.usd
    action_id "serve.subpoena"
  }
  discovery-motion-quash-subpoena "File Motion to Quash or Modify a Subpoena — within the later of 10 days after receipt or an ALJ-extended period (Rule 210.32(d))" -> discovery-open {
    authority cite cfr210.32.d
    effort 12.hours
    cost 5_000.usd
    deadline 10.days {
      extendable true
      extension_authority "ALJ-extended period"
      note "19 CFR 210.32(d). The rule text does not itself state an automatic waiver-on-lateness consequence, so no waiver flag is asserted for a late motion to quash — contrast the RFA trap above."
    }
    duration { min 1.5.days, mode 5.days, max 10.days }
    action_id "file.motion.quash"
  }
  discovery-take-deposition "Take Deposition (7-hour day cap; 20 fact depositions per side, 10 for Commission staff, Rule 210.28)" -> discovery-open {
    authority cite cfr210.28.limits
    effort 12.hours
    cost 3_500.usd
    action_id "take.deposition"
  }
  discovery-file-privilege-log "File Privilege Log for withheld material within 10 days (Rule 210.27(e))" -> discovery-open {
    authority cite cfr210.27.e
    effort 4.hours
    cost 300.usd
    deadline 10.days {
      extendable true
      extension_authority "good cause"
      note "19 CFR 210.27(e): privilege log due 10 days after the response listing each withheld item's date, authors, recipients, subject matter, and privilege type. A missed log is sanction exposure under 210.33(a), not an automatic waiver — the pack deliberately declines to invent a hard waiver flag the regulatory text does not itself state."
    }
    duration { min 1.5.days, mode 5.days, max 10.days }
    action_id "file.privilege-log"
  }
  discovery-meet-and-confer "Meet and Confer on Discovery Dispute" -> discovery-open {
    authority cite cfr210.33.a
    effort 2.hours
    cost 800.usd
    action_id "confer.meet-and-confer"
  }
  _ "File Motion to Compel Discovery (Rule 210.33(a))" -> order-compelling-discovery {
    authority cite cfr210.33.a
    effort 14.hours
    cost 5_000.usd
    action_id "file.motion.compel"
  }
  _ "Designate Material as Confidential Business Information (Rule 210.5)" -> cbi-designated {
    authority cite cfr210.5.disclosure
    effort 1.hours
    cost 0.usd
    action_id "designate.cbi"
  }
  _ "File Public (Redacted) Version of a confidential submission within 30 days (Rule 210.5)" -> public-version-filed {
    authority cite cfr210.5.public-version
    effort 5.hours
    cost 500.usd
    deadline 30.days {
      extendable true
      extension_authority "good cause"
      note "19 CFR 210.5: public version due within 30 days of the confidential filing absent a good-cause extension."
    }
    duration { min 4.5.days, mode 15.days, max 30.days }
    valence good
    action_id "file.public-version"
  }
  _ "Discovery record complete — case proceeds toward the summary-determination window and hearing (Rule 210.51(a))" -> prehearing {
    authority cite cfr210.51.a
    effort 0.hours
    duration { min 120.days, mode 270.days, max 420.days }
    note "Duration: estimate. Discovery in a § 337 investigation typically runs several months within the 12-18 month target-date schedule the ALJ sets under 19 CFR 210.51(a); not a measured statistic for this matter."
  }
}

